  {
   "id": "W_fvAa7eu8UJ",
   "from": "Alex Brown",
   "author": "c8fe4075ec631c03",
   "date": "2012-12-16T02:07:37Z",
   "subject": "reactivePlot that has no output in ui.R causes error : diagnosis and suggested fix supplied.",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "I use reactiveUI to selected between UI types (javascript and rendered).<div><br></div><div>This means that there can be server reactivePlot elements that are not matched by plotOutputs in the ui. (at any given time).</div><div><br></div><div>a simple example: </div><div><br></div><div><font color=\"#333333\" face=\"Consolas, Liberation Mono, Courier, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">output$myPlot &lt;- reactivePlot(function() {})</span></font></div><div><br></div><div>Where</div><div><br></div><div><div><font color=\"#333333\" face=\"Consolas, Liberation Mono, Courier, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">plotOutput(&quot;myPlot&quot;)</span></font></div><div><br></div></div><div>Should NOT exist.</div><div><br></div><div>(of course my real plot has actual stuff in, but it doesn&#39;t matter, because it&#39;s not invoked anyway).</div><div><br></div><div>When you execute such a thing on a shiny server it says:</div><div><br></div><div>&quot;Error in if (width &lt;= 0 || height &lt;= 0) return(NULL) : </div><div>  missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed.&quot;</div><div><br></div><div>This code matches a snipper in shinywrappers.R.</div><div><br></div><div>width and height start out as (default) &quot;auto&quot; but are replaced by </div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">shinyapp</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">$</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">session</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">$</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">get</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">paste</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">prefix</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\"> name</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">&#39;_width&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\"> sep</span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">&#39;&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">));</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\">etc.</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre\"><br></span></div><div>at invocation of the lambda returned by reactivePlot, but before it invokes the actual myPlot function.</div><div> <br></div><div>I suspect the problem is that shiny is not checking to see if this call to session$get fails (which it must).</div><div><br></div><div>Expected behaviour:</div><div><br></div><div>no error message</div><div><br></div><div>Suggested implementation:</div><div><pre><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\"><br></span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">if</span> <span>(is.null(width) || is.null(height) || </span>width <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">&lt;=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">0</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">||</span> height <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">&lt;=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">0</span><span>)</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;padding-left:10px\">      <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">return</span><span>(</span><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">NULL</span><span>)</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;padding-left:10px\"><span><br></span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Alternative implementation:</font></span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Ask session$get to see if the plot itself exists and bail if it doesn&#39;t.</font></span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Note that this issue also means that a single plot cannot be re-used by multiple output points, which has been noted elsewhere.  I don&#39;t know if this is important.</font></span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Thanks!</font></span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">-Alex Brown</font></span></div></pre></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
