    [
     3,
     "<br><br>On Monday, December 17, 2012 10:38:28 AM UTC-8, Joe Cheng [RStudio] wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Hi Alex, thanks for pointing this out. Just to clarify the severity of the bug, there&#39;s no side effect other than an error message being printed at the console, right? i.e. it doesn&#39;t affect the correct operation of the rest of the application?<div>\r\n<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sat, Dec 15, 2012 at 6:07 PM, Alex Brown <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">alexb...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\nI use reactiveUI to selected between UI types (javascript and rendered).<div><br></div><div>This means that there can be server reactivePlot elements that are not matched by plotOutputs in the ui. (at any given time).</div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>a simple example: </div><div><br></div><div><font color=\"#333333\" face=\"Consolas, Liberation Mono, Courier, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">output$myPlot &lt;- reactivePlot(function() {})</span></font></div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>Where</div><div><br></div><div><div><font color=\"#333333\" face=\"Consolas, Liberation Mono, Courier, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">plotOutput(&quot;myPlot&quot;)</span></font></div>\r\n<div><br></div></div><div>Should NOT exist.</div><div><br></div><div>(of course my real plot has actual stuff in, but it doesn&#39;t matter, because it&#39;s not invoked anyway).</div><div><br></div><div>When you execute such a thing on a shiny server it says:</div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>&quot;Error in if (width &lt;= 0 || height &lt;= 0) return(NULL) : </div><div>  missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed.&quot;</div><div><br></div><div>This code matches a snipper in shinywrappers.R.</div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>width and height start out as (default) &quot;auto&quot; but are replaced by </div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br>\r\n</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">shinyapp</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">$</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">session</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">$</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">get</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">paste</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">prefix</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\"> name</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">&#39;_width&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\"> sep</span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">&#39;&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">));</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\">etc.</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br>\r\n</span></div><div>at invocation of the lambda returned by reactivePlot, but before it invokes the actual myPlot function.</div><div> <br></div><div>I suspect the problem is that shiny is not checking to see if this call to session$get fails (which it must).</div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>Expected behaviour:</div><div><br></div><div>no error message</div><div><br></div><div>Suggested implementation:</div><div><pre><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;padding-left:10px\">\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold\"><br></span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">if</span> <span>(is.null(width) || is.null(height) || </span>width <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">&lt;=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">0</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">||</span> height <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">&lt;=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">0</span><span>)</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;padding-left:10px\">      <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">return</span><span>(</span><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">NULL</span><span>)</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;padding-left:10px\"><span><br></span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Alternative implementation:</font></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Ask session$get to see if the plot itself exists and bail if it doesn&#39;t.</font></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Note that this issue also means that a single plot cannot be re-used by multiple output points, which has been noted elsewhere.  I don&#39;t know if this is important.</font></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Thanks!</font></span></div>\r\n<span><font color=\"#888888\"><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">-Alex Brown</font></span></div>\r\n</font></span></pre></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n</blockquote>"
    ]
   ]
